#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:2
msgid "Set up SSH keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:3
msgid "*Connect to SEPAL without entering your account password*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:5
msgid ""
"Create an SSH key on your computer and register its public part in SEPAL."
" You can then use it with any SSH client, including the tools described "
"in :doc:`../developers/ssh_session`. If you already have a key on your "
"computer, skip the first step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:10
msgid ""
"In a **local** terminal (PowerShell on Windows, Terminal on macOS or "
"Linux), create a key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:17
msgid ""
"Accept the default location and choose a passphrase. Do not overwrite an "
"existing key. This creates a private key, ``id_ed25519``, and a public "
"key, ``id_ed25519.pub``, in your user's ``.ssh`` folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:20
msgid ""
"In SEPAL, open your user menu, select **SSH keys**, then **Add**. Select "
"or drop the ``id_ed25519.pub`` file, or paste its contents into **Public "
"key**. Give it a recognizable **Name**, then select **Add**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:20
msgid "SEPAL SSH keys panel with the Add button at the lower left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:20
msgid "Add SSH key dialog with public key file, public key and name fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:36
msgid ""
"Connect to your SEPAL session using your SSH client. SSH uses the default"
" key automatically; you may be prompted for its passphrase. If you saved "
"the key elsewhere, add ``IdentityFile /path/to/your/private/key`` to the "
"host's SSH configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/ssh_keys.rst:43
msgid ""
"Upload only the public ``.pub`` file. Keep the private key on your "
"computer. On Windows, use the key and configuration belonging to the SSH "
"client used by VS Code; keys created inside WSL are stored separately "
"from Windows keys."
msgstr ""

